THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

The MIT terms above cover the code, the corpus metadata in data/corpus.json,
and the analysis in this repository.

They do not cover the policy documents themselves. The files in data/text/ and
data/extracts/ are text of instruments published by their issuing authorities
— SDAIA, SFDA, NCA, NDMO, CST, the Ministry of Health, the Saudi Health
Council, CBAHI, WHO, ITU-T and the US Department of Health and Human Services.
Copyright in those documents remains with their issuers. They are reproduced
here so that the reported figures are reproducible without network access to
hosts that block automated retrieval, and each carries a link to its official
source in data/corpus.json. Anyone relying on an instrument should read it at
that source.

All patient data in data/samples/ is synthetic. No real patient, clinician or
facility record is represented.
